 in Greek mythology.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7c77-964c-c988c58c5e3d","description":"Leto","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7baf-a15f-a99cf333449c","description":"Diana","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-76aa-b5b0-e8691369a829","description":"Helen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7bb9-b258-29ffebb72190","description":"Aphrodite","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7eb8-91b3-ba67a4e591fd","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which Pig Latin word is used to reject or cancel a statement?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Ixnay comes from \u201cnix,\u201d an informal word meaning to reject or prohibit; Pig Latin moves the opening consonant sound to the end and adds \u201cay.\u201d","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-786e-9ccc-b372f30c7c9e","description":"Ixnay","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7c29-9ee3-db91b1fe2fa5","description":"Epay","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-74a6-95e5-d445c4bff7cc","description":"Ocklay","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-74a9-9087-7203d404fbd0","description":"Oopstay","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7906-85ca-7ab1b1eeb1ee","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which Greek god invented the shepherd\'s flute and had a musical contest with Apollo?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Pan\u2019s reed pipes are commonly called panpipes. In the musical contest, Apollo played the lyre.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7b02-a64b-b65c5dc2fd77","description":"Pan","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7504-83b5-24b24123ed4d","description":"Zeus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7195-b14f-79cf8f870140","description":"Artemis","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7a4f-b016-448e25c778e0","description":"Athena","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-77db-ac92-8807ab310cb2","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c846499