stion":"Which philosopher famously said \'Even while they teach, men learn\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Seneca the Younger was a Roman statesman as well as a philosopher; his moral essays and letters remain among his best-known works.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7e79-badc-d0e02e2837fb","description":"Seneca the Younger","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-78c7-bcdd-51b521cd489e","description":"Thomas Hobbes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7617-987b-4b4a91da9822","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-770e-816d-227db49dc33f","description":"Socrates","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7734-b0c3-a77c65956e1d","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Who was the ancient Egyptian goddess of the sky and queen of heaven ?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Hathor was worshipped as a sky goddess and known as the Lady of Heaven. She was also associated with love, music, and motherhood.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7314-b913-e8585d85644e","description":"Hathor","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-78e9-ad1e-1bc1dcbb469a","description":"Isis","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7153-8672-849a1aa0f372","description":"Set","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-796d-a3f4-da7c24515780","description":"Horus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-77cc-9504-7574a5ea853f","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is a wide cuff that is folded back and fastened with a cuff link called?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"French cuffs are traditionally considered more formal than button-fastened cuffs and use separate cuff links rather than sewn-on buttons.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-719d-9080-b55f7501cc36","description":"A French cuff","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-74c4-be90-33a4aebf11ea","description":"A button cuff","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7c07-bedc-364e1140ecc5","description":"A barrel cuff","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-744a-852a-9c15ab51479b","description":"A saville cuff","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-71be-b6c2-253626a3c7f5","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'What is rational is actual and what is actual is rational\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The line appears in the preface to Hegel\u2019s Philosophy of Right, where he explored the relationship between reason and the world.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7aa4-a2fa-224d9e447286","description":"G. W. F. Hegel","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7469-a79b-421cd9c6f42c","description":"William of Ockham","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7708-bba5-2eeccbb7ae16","description":"Bertrand Russell","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7f52-9c80-51c1b22dd4ac","description":"Democritus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-79d6-a2ae-5cfe60f94be1","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"In 1982, which member of the British royal family gave birth to Prince William?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Princess Diana and Charles also had a younger son, Prince Harry, born in 1984.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7882-9364-ad5d3476d50b","description":"Princess Diana","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7a8f-8344-0696ac16db5b","description":"Queen Elizabeth II","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7f9c-8d37-eace0a1ecb96","description":"Camilla Parker Bowles","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7d25-8d99-c300bbe73ee8","description":"Sarah Ferguson","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7cda-837a-fdf7d5be353d","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Berber is a language spoken in which of these countries?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Berber languages are also known as Amazigh, and Morocco recognizes Tamazight as an official language.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7d29-9af9-78319b85b8d1","description":"Morocco","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7834-bd2d-360a709f67a5","description":"Kenya","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7712-b93c-d56be9f550fb","description":"Tanzania","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7fac-80b7-19fee6f1a349","description":"Sri Lanka","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7926-93cf-10ceb8c84fc9","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'Whereof one cannot speak, thereof one must be silent\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Ludwig Wittgenstein\u2019s Tractatus Logico-Philosophicus explores the limits of language and thought.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7c40-b6c5-77e126b3d915","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7a2e-8f71-05be491055b7","description":"William of Ockham","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7d81-9613-6d37a3d4f7aa","description":"Bertrand Russell","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-741e-8922-3c919381e00f","description":"Immanuel Kant","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7c63-b62c-27d3e921bf97","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which of these Latin phrases means \'Overcome evil with good\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Bono malum superate uses a plural command form, addressing more than one person, and echoes the injunction in Romans 12:21.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7345-b866-8ba4dd831970","description":"Bono malum superate","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-79f4-8e2d-2a52ff6d242d","description":"Bona fide","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-73d8-b7c7-fff0e8734b9c","description":"Humilitas occidit superbiam","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7323-a560-403957c0d940","description":"Fortiter et fideliter","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7acc-9830-4cee7e1c816f","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'There is only one thing a philosopher can be relied upon to do, and that is to contradict other philosophers\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"William James was also a pioneering psychologist. His work helped shape pragmatism, which evaluates ideas partly by their practical consequences.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-754a-98d1-37b214758ddb","description":"William James","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-761e-8005-9d5572342acd","description":"Thomas Hobbes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7017-9dca-4a6373baf91f","description":"Socrates","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-705a-987a-23f8364a4f9f","description":"Martin Heidegger","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-74a6-bd2b-aa8bedfcc62a","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the shortest verse in the Bible?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Jesus wept is John 11:35, which describes Jesus mourning at Lazarus\u2019s tomb. It is commonly cited as the shortest verse in English-language Bibles.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7e7e-adbc-b03f35779621","description":"Jesus wept","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-764f-a06d-8f039df61bad","description":"God spoke","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7bd9-9ff2-bdb4a8eb4be9","description":"No more","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7a8c-9cdb-d751d76fb3e5","description":"Hallelujah","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7339-99b7-0df15d63e20a","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"In 2002, which US city saw a number of coordinated sniper killings?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The 2002 Beltway sniper attacks took place across the Washington metropolitan area, including suburbs in Maryland and Virginia.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7bd0-a067-de463c62700a","description":"Washington, D.C.","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7f49-98f6-0a16bd742ee0","description":"New York City","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7568-a4ae-b19883e41de5","description":"Los Angeles","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-786a-97d5-d16e86cbbf1a","description":"Chicago","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7c68-88d8-a88c26358a8b","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"How does that Latin phrase \'Pax vobiscum\' translate into English?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"\u201cPeace be with you\u201d is a traditional Christian liturgical greeting, often used during worship.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7a39-875a-1575e514c3fa","description":"Peace be with you","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-71a5-8030-6e6c8959f696","description":"In good faith","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-747e-9789-c504e516f386","description":"And you, Brutus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7cdb-82b1-59ab9abc8680","description":"Nothing is arduous for the willing","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-714a-81b0-d719a31e625e","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"How does that Latin phrase \'Tempora mutantur et nos mutamur in illis\' translate into English?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"\'Tempora mutantur, et nos mutamur in illis\' means times change and we change with them.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7ec2-9d18-fba1e97992e3","description":"The times are changing, and we change with them","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7f87-a1d8-18a3d33d1bb1","description":"What is said is done","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7d24-865e-04f2a1170971","description":"The act done by me against my will is not my act","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7d80-b756-d31a1ad01e94","description":"Fortune favors the bold","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7744-94e3-688860474893","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the national animal of Scotland?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The unicorn appears as a supporter on Scotland\u2019s royal coat of arms, often shown chained because it was regarded as wild and untamable.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-71f4-b0b6-103b3248f179","description":"Unicorn","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-782b-a1b5-5f008fd57ca4","description":"Lion","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-71fd-b303-23be6beb4225","description":"Dragon","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-707d-b8aa-c567c7258a61","description":"Horse","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7526-8359-caf0120a0a24","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What charity organization works to protect the rights of indigenous and tribal peoples?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Survival International campaigns against the forced displacement of Indigenous peoples and defends their rights to their lands and ways of life.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7b9c-9f63-17af4b9387db","description":"Survival International","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7956-8a34-bcc39b0794ba","description":"Greenpeace","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7c1e-ae42-d09b8a424828","description":"Amnesty International","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7db5-84d8-83e4bba54236","description":"The Nature Conservancy","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-76f2-b473-491d501aab49","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'It is undesirable to believe a proposition when there is no ground whatever for supposing it true\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Bertrand Russell received the Nobel Prize in Literature for his varied writings, which championed humanitarian ideals and freedom of thought.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7a95-946a-581e2fc51760","description":"Bertrand Russell","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-75f0-991b-550500b16b92","description":"Thomas Hobbes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-759b-bf99-33f2de8200e9","description":"Jean-Jacques Rousseau","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7a5f-95cc-40497b34b4e0","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7fa2-a2e3-ce2621332e9b","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which Norse god acts as the watchman of the gods, guarding the rainbow bridge Bifr\u00f6st?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Heimdall is also described as having exceptionally sharp senses; some accounts say he can hear grass growing.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-74c1-a236-6057b1f14fd2","description":"Heimdall","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7293-b845-a6345a14ceaf","description":"Thor","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7611-b4c8-fd0864cb4fb5","description":"Baldur","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-749a-9dc0-3af1b89ae25b","description":"Tyr","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7732-8888-1d73a3577c87","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'God is not willing to do everything, and thus take away our free will and that share of glory which belongs to us\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Niccolo Machiavelli discusses the balance between fortune and human agency in The Prince, where this line appears.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7f06-9f4a-c98e20d020ab","description":"Niccolo Machiavelli","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7230-814a-893694d4dbf0","description":"Jean-Paul Sartre","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7d18-a014-0150d03bedbc","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-771f-b7b4-b76211baa9da","description":"Karl Marx","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7fef-b6d2-51c7042ec33a","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which of these Latin phrases means \'Wisdom is power\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"In Sapientia potentia est, sapientia is the subject, potentia means power, and est is the verb meaning \u201cis.\u201d","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7338-b499-d9134779e696","description":"Sapientia potentia est","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7e59-ad9a-a2e0500d382b","description":"Hodie mihi, cras tibi","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7d92-bd54-11d4570b5355","description":"Ego te provoco","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-77e8-8c26-94bb3fa42f52","description":"Melita, domi adsum","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7191-a816-eb3a785a3a25","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which of the following describes John Dalton?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"John Dalton proposed that matter is made of indivisible atoms, with each element having its own type. His ideas helped lay the groundwork for modern chemistry.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-72cc-9a92-64e37d32e58e","description":"Chemist and physicist who ade contributions to atomic theory.","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7e71-8a8e-65e578a7a0e8","description":"Industrialist who revolutionised mass-production techniques.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7ceb-9c42-08e1a224a8cf","description":"Confirmed the theory that Earth revolves around The Sun.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7c4c-b77f-18b27a863275","description":"38th President of the US.","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-70f0-b674-338a59f87ed0","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the name of the flag flown on a short pole at the bow of a ship?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A jack is flown at the bow, while a ship\u2019s ensign is generally flown at the stern; a burgee commonly identifies a yacht club.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7d9c-8af9-8029d4f5d18f","description":"Jack","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7abf-8c27-a63954d5f76a","description":"Ensign","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-71e2-a801-c7837ae1cd7c","description":"Pennant","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7a3b-b98d-f36321983d02","description":"Burgee","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-72d4-91b5-b130a0575558","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"How does that Latin phrase \'Actus me invito factus non est meus actus\' translate into English?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The phrase means \u201cThe act done by me against my will is not my act,\u201d expressing the legal principle that criminal responsibility generally requires voluntary conduct.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7ab8-b32f-fcc33312a588","description":"The act done by me against my will is not my act","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-79e9-ab65-141c18aa2e70","description":"To act accidentally is not to act at all","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7151-90f2-a5b4d3d44818","description":"Act as if you are always being watched","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7ef6-972e-27827dab8375","description":"The act of an honest man cannot be questioned","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-74d7-a4d2-1bbf920c2972","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the name of the US Military\'s highest award for valor in combat?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Medal of Honor is the nation\u2019s highest military decoration, reserved for conspicuous gallantry and intrepidity at risk of life, above and beyond the call of duty.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7780-908a-723518a82899","description":"Medal of Honor","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7f40-aa59-2cf32d24b25b","description":"Purple Heart","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7f06-a105-83a8d110ab29","description":"Bronze Star","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-771d-925d-5b5f5f85fc14","description":"Silver Star","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7f82-890f-b753f047de35","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'We live in the best of all possible worlds\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Leibniz argued that a perfect God would create the best possible world among all possible worlds. Voltaire later satirized that optimism in Candide.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-763b-a40a-fd94f33db45b","description":"Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-78b6-a943-a02eb7da3ac9","description":"Thomas Hobbes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7e10-aa12-9c61cc4a426a","description":"Denis Diderot","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7725-b65c-cd2c7eccea87","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-70a7-99ea-233911327707","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the name of the first month of the year in the Islamic calendar?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Muharram is one of four sacred months in Islam. Its name is commonly understood to mean \u201cforbidden,\u201d reflecting a traditional prohibition on warfare during the month.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7a34-8a59-8b545afbac24","description":"Muharram","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-788e-a0e4-5c31920c2833","description":"Ramadan","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7af5-bbff-c549e9c814c6","description":"Shawwal","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7397-ad17-89340399ab68","description":"Jumada Al-Awwal","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7a9d-a3be-b4a67dc9c429","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which country had its first female prime minister, Kim Campbell, serve in 1993?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Canada\u2019s Kim Campbell served for only 132 days before the Progressive Conservatives lost the 1993 federal election.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7a92-a40a-77b03bffccf6","description":"Canada","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7b60-87b5-dfc8d11260d6","description":"United States","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7af6-be0a-c744ad33f460","description":"United Kingdom","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-75d7-8f3a-f449eb13305e","description":"Australia","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7a94-8a14-e0082168904b","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"The language \'Ta\u02bdizzi-Adeni Arabic\' belongs to which language family?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Afroasiatic includes the Semitic languages as well as branches such as Berber, Cushitic, and Chadic.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-71b6-8587-42a029ea5b35","description":"Afroasiatic","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7c36-938b-123cb01299e4","description":"Austronesian","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7f4a-a3d4-29c9f7ab3ed8","description":"Kra\u2013Dai","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7e87-a822-8062524d1dc4","description":"Koreanic","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7385-8d22-25f3db4e8fa3","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"In what animal form did Zeus seduce Europa?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Zeus appeared as a bull and carried Europa to Crete, where their son Minos became a legendary king.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7c5d-81cb-5a464cb23d77","description":"Bull","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-763a-8689-b5fc423ee7e7","description":"Horse","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-72bf-a924-96bb19a8dd94","description":"Dolphin","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-72ed-9366-523482f1b507","description":"Eagle","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7bc2-af81-33cf83ac7568","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"The language \'Kinyarwanda\' belongs to which language family?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Kinyarwanda is a Bantu language, and Bantu languages form a major branch of the Niger\u2013Congo family. It is spoken throughout Rwanda.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7e54-8bdd-1e489d40ab15","description":"Niger\u2013Congo","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7f2e-ae5a-ae840fc73833","description":"Uralic","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7e6c-9e9a-80ffd52cfe6e","description":"Austronesian","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7918-955d-e27f8f324642","description":"Dravidian","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7c46-a87e-60762d26cbb5","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"The language \'Sudanese Arabic\' belongs to which language family?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Afroasiatic includes the Semitic branch, which contains Arabic as well as Hebrew and Aramaic.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7cc5-8096-03ce1ded94f7","description":"Afroasiatic","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-773f-85e1-6b7cffbb7419","description":"Kra\u2013Dai","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-764a-8696-ee44ca3e8f20","description":"Niger\u2013Congo","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-782f-8d3c-fac77667ff1b","description":"Austronesian","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7c8a-aa39-2bf4fbe7711c","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the name of the Hindu scripture that contains the dialogue between Krishna and Arjuna?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Bhagavad Gita is part of the Mahabharata, framed as a conversation just before battle. It is distinct from the Upanishads, the Ramayana, and the Puranas.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7afe-8d9a-e942370452d6","description":"The Bhagavad Gita","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-75d2-bdbf-29573b09e2df","description":"The Upanishads","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-71c6-8165-01c545f5dcf4","description":"The Ramayana","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7e1b-9dae-2f41e39f18e6","description":"The Puranas","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7132-844d-b003ac89a718","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the name of the Islamic call to prayer?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The adhan is the call to prayer recited by the muezzin to summon Muslims.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7c86-b831-6bd115fb8921","description":"Adhan","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7c24-b222-92a480bc1451","description":"Iqama","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-71a1-8758-344f84aeee5b","description":"Niqab","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7760-a3a9-0118f9ba05b6","description":"Wudu","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7abf-addb-8ce8fac82be5","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the name of the Hindu festival of colors?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Holi is also known as the spring festival; many communities light bonfires on the eve of the celebration.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-748f-87a3-626cd87a6fe3","description":"Holi","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-74fe-9c1d-8f92780a1fd0","description":"Diwali","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-74df-988c-9d84c63e4e71","description":"Dusshera","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-71a3-ad50-7dac9bbb98eb","description":"Navaratri","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7778-9c7b-f90f64bcc5ee","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which Latin music legend is known for her signature fruity hat?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Carmen Miranda was a Brazilian singer and actress who became an international star in Hollywood musicals.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373c-77ba-a486-381c13176330","description":"Carmen Miranda","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7b6c-8bf1-ef68f0dd886c","description":"Gloria Estefan","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-76aa-b3b4-135af1c779e6","description":"Celia Cruz","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7adb-92c4-d5abb5b6ddd3","description":"Jennifer Lopez","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373c-7f41-b552-160c62d8f999","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'Man is born free, but is everywhere in chains\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Jean-Jacques Rousseau opens The Social Contract with this line, setting up his argument about political authority and freedom.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373d-7fdf-8bdc-36b937386a48","description":"Jean-Jacques Rousseau","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-7eaa-a173-d4caf16c37f1","description":"Jean-Paul Sartre","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-7531-b54b-5c72f05595c7","description":"Spinoza","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-7f62-8b35-553f176c0a10","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-7d38-a1e6-637912fb0c67","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which of these Latin phrases means \'Lead in order to serve, not in order to rule\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Praesis ut prosis ne ut imperes frames leadership as a duty to help others, rather than a license to command.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373d-7ae7-8cec-de5db31b81ad","description":"Praesis ut prosis ne ut imperes","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-7ee5-8486-a544f08745a7","description":"Libertas perfundet omnia luce","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-7c54-b6ac-6ad6c61a8b82","description":"Non loqui sed facere","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-74e8-842c-fb2742edceea","description":"Carpe diem","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-7550-889c-7269bef8df21","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What organisation is based in the Lubjlyanka building?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The FSB is Russia\'s domestic security and counterintelligence agency, and it succeeded the KGB after the Soviet Union dissolved.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373d-7bd9-a9e9-ed9cfda914b7","description":"The FSB","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-710b-b40b-5dc832a9e7ec","description":"The EU","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-7eb3-bd9a-74ffdfce3ec4","description":"The WHO","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-78e8-8068-6a6f7c0a45d2","description":"Interpol","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-7d09-a46e-efbfe46d06d3","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which official is first in the statutory line to act as President if both the President and Vice President can no longer serve?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Presidential Succession Act places the Speaker of the House ahead of cabinet officials in the succession order.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373d-778e-8f81-7dd3d8ebb686","description":"The Speaker of the House","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-775a-a604-a9a90196afd0","description":"The Secretary of State","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-7d12-9673-8470e4649abe","description":"The Secretary of Defense","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-713f-9161-4924369c7528","description":"The Attorney General","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-7e2c-b57e-29aa6e1f429d","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which of these languages would you find spoken in Pakistan?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"In Pakistan, Punjabi is commonly written in the Shahmukhi script, which is based on the Perso-Arabic alphabet.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373d-79db-8c8f-3023caeaca4f","description":"Punjabi","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9