 places it in the Indo-European family.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373d-798d-b9aa-799131a08139","description":"Indo-European","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-7c35-9957-008130488115","description":"Kra\u2013Dai","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-70c7-a460-d4e435d9a29b","description":"Japonic","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-7e2e-b8a4-e8a0ef2368ae","description":"Afroasiatic","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-7688-86ba-afc2bddecf96","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"Which philosopher famously said \'It is wrong always, everywhere and for everyone, to believe anything upon insufficient evidence\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"W. K. Clifford argued that careless beliefs can shape actions and spread harm beyond the person who holds them.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373d-760b-844c-ebcdb29e8387","description":"W. K. Clifford","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-7729-add2-654cf4f4eefd","description":"Thomas Hobbes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-702a-9053-ad7348cdd22f","description":"Ludwig Wittgenstein","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-7c7e-8cec-b7f3ef692f33","description":"Epictetus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-7703-9266-61e6658279f2","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7dd6-93ca-116c8464996a","question":"What is the Portuguese word for \'five\'?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Cinco is also the Spanish word for five, reflecting the languages\u2019 shared Latin roots.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-373d-726f-891a-55c6c4dfaad7","description":"Cinco","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-77ea-8f06-3813c276a33e","description":"Vijf","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-7705-b3b3-b3d687403c7e","description":"F\u00fcnf","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-708d-9e3b-0c00cb63d787","description":"Oito","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-373d-7020-8cc2-1f7a6337339c","locale":"en-US","ca